# console-both.list -- ship every console driver and let the machine choose.
#
# THE CONSOLE IS A RUNTIME CHOICE, NOT A BUILD VARIANT.  `vidsel' (md.s) probes
# for a video board at boot and patches init's argv[2] to name the driver to
# load, falling back to the serial redirect.  One kernel binary therefore serves
# serial, LR and HR machines, and these fragments only decide which drivers are
# PRESENT to be chosen.  Never build a per-console kernel.
#
# This is what a general distribution should ship -- it boots correctly on any
# machine and the whole console payload is ~10 KB.  console-lr / console-hr exist
# only to trim an image for a known-hardware install.
#
# The three fragments are the kernel repository's (os/dist/lists there): it
# links the drivers, so it defines the components and cuts their packages.  They
# resolve here through the same search path as the drivers they stage.
include	lists/console-serial.list
include	lists/console-lr.list
include	lists/console-hr.list
